{
  "task_id": "adaptive-cruise-control",
  "top_k": 5,
  "requirements": [
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_a2339cb73880586edca7",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/adaptive-cruise-control/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 1,
        "line_end": 1,
        "exact_text": "You need to implement an Adaptive Cruise Control (ACC) simulation that maintains the set speed (30m/s) when no vehicles are detected ahead, and automatically adjusts speed to maintain a safe following distance when a vehicle is detected ahead. The targets are: speed rise time <10s, speed overshoot <5%, speed steady-state error <0.5 m/s, distance steady-state error <2m, minimum distance >5m, control duration 150s. Also consider the constraints: initial speed ~0 m/s, acceleration limits [-8.0, 3.0] m/s^2, time headway 1.5s, minimum gap 10.0m, emergency TTC threshold 3.0s, timestep 0.1s. Data is available in vehicle_params.yaml(Vehicle specs and ACC settings)  and sensor_data.csv (1501 rows (t=0-150s) with columns: time, ego_speed, lead_speed, distance, collected from real-world driving).\n",
        "source_sha256": "c5def70c3ccb7a14cc3da61daed59eb138f5782e75d787c5f4ad1223feb75124",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_c20ca4f8c2d94869287e",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/adaptive-cruise-control/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 4,
        "line_end": 4,
        "exact_text": "First, create pid_controller.py to implement the PID controller. Then, create acc_system.py to implement the ACC system and simulation.py to run the vehicle simulation. Next, tune the PID parameters for speed and distance control, saving results in tuning_results.yaml. Finally, run 150s simulations, producing simulation_results.csv and acc_report.md.\n",
        "source_sha256": "c5def70c3ccb7a14cc3da61daed59eb138f5782e75d787c5f4ad1223feb75124",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_5e82cb3841b2ce64c794",
      "requirement_type": "OUTPUT_PATH",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/adaptive-cruise-control/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 7,
        "line_end": 7,
        "exact_text": "Examples output format:\n",
        "source_sha256": "c5def70c3ccb7a14cc3da61daed59eb138f5782e75d787c5f4ad1223feb75124",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_6ef131edf95cca91d9d0",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/adaptive-cruise-control/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 9,
        "line_end": 12,
        "exact_text": "pid_controller.py:\nClass: PIDController\nConstructor: __init__(self, kp, ki, kd)\nMethods: reset(), compute(error, dt) returns float\n",
        "source_sha256": "c5def70c3ccb7a14cc3da61daed59eb138f5782e75d787c5f4ad1223feb75124",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_9ff7b93399c0fc375531",
      "requirement_type": "DOMAIN_ACTION",
      "criticality": "CORE",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/adaptive-cruise-control/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 14,
        "line_end": 18,
        "exact_text": "acc_system.py:\nClass: AdaptiveCruiseControl\nConstructor: __init__(self, config) where config is nested dict from vehicle_params.yaml (e.g., config['acc_settings']['set_speed'])\nMethod: compute(ego_speed, lead_speed, distance, dt) returns tuple (acceleration_cmd, mode, distance_error)\nMode selection: 'cruise' when lead_speed is None, 'emergency' when TTC < threshold, 'follow' when lead vehicle present\n",
        "source_sha256": "c5def70c3ccb7a14cc3da61daed59eb138f5782e75d787c5f4ad1223feb75124",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    },
    {
      "requirement_id": "req_32701e799a3119f16fa5",
      "requirement_type": "FORMAT",
      "criticality": "HARD",
      "provenance": {
        "source_file": "tasks/adaptive-cruise-control/instruction.md",
        "source_type": "instruction",
        "line_start": 20,
        "line_end": 23,
        "exact_text": "simulation.py:\nRead PID gains from tuning_results.yaml file at runtime.\nDo not embed auto-tuning logic because gains should be loaded from the yaml file.\nUses sensor_data.csv for lead vehicle data (lead_speed, distance).\n",
        "source_sha256": "c5def70c3ccb7a14cc3da61daed59eb138f5782e75d787c5f4ad1223feb75124",
        "extraction_rule": "actionable_paragraph"
      }
    }
  ],
